---
title: Turkey Burgers
description: Juicy seasoned turkey burger patties — grill, skillet, or oven — ready in about 20 minutes.
source: https://tastesbetterfromscratch.com/turkey-burgers/
author: Lauren Allen (Tastes Better From Scratch)
servings: 4
prep time: 10 minutes
cook time: 10 minutes
time required: 20 minutes
course: main
cuisine: American
tags:
  - turkey
  - burgers
  - grill
  - quick
---

> Adapted from Tastes Better From Scratch. Freeze patties 20 minutes before grilling so they hold their shape. Mixture will be wet.

In a #mixing bowl{}, gently combine @lean ground turkey{1%lb}, @garlic powder{1/2%tsp}, @onion powder{1/2%tsp}, @ketchup{1 1/2%tbsp}, @Dijon mustard{1%tbsp}, @Worcestershire sauce{1%tsp}, @salt{3/4%tsp}, @black pepper{1/2%tsp}, @bread crumbs{1/3%cup}, and @egg{1} just until combined — do not overmix.

Shape into 4 patties about 1/2-inch thick. Press a thumb depression in the center of each. Place on a parchment-lined plate and freeze for ~{20%minutes}.

== Grill ==

Clean and grease #grill{} grates; heat to medium-high. Grill a few minutes per side until 160°F.

== Skillet ==

Heat oil or spray in a #nonstick skillet{} over medium-high. Cook ~{4-5%minutes} per side.

== Oven ==

Bake at 375°F for ~{25-30%minutes}, then sear 2 minutes per side in a hot pan.

Serve on @hamburger buns{4} with condiments (ketchup, mustard, mayo, BBQ) and toppings (lettuce, tomato, onion, pickles, avocado, bacon, mushrooms, jalapeños) as desired.
